From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 16:22:20 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] webOS: Add Teams voice calling for the webOS Phone app

Add 1:1 Teams voice calls for personal (Teams for Life) accounts on
webOS, driven by the stock Phone app:

- teams_calling.c/.h: parse the NGC call notifications from the Trouter
  (SDP offer, MS-TURN relay, control links), track call state, and
  answer, reject, hang up and dial over the call control plane. The
  audio runs in the separate teams_media engine (from
  luneos-synergy-connectors), one process per call, spawned from
  TEAMS_MEDIA_BIN and driven over its stdin/stdout. Its stdin is a
  socket written with MSG_NOSIGNAL, so an engine that dies cannot take
  the messaging service down with SIGPIPE; it is reaped with a child
  watch, and a call whose engine exits is ended. Freeing a call stops
  its engine, and an attach response for a call that has ended is
  ignored. While a call is in progress a second incoming call is turned
  away and a dial is refused. Calls placed from the user's other
  devices are not shown. A hangup ends the call through its
  conversation controller, which a placed call gets from the cpconv
  response. languageId and clientLocation come from the locale, with
  "en-us" and "NL" when it has no country. Calls are voice only.
- teams_call_luna.c/.h: the com.palm.teams.call luna-service2 service
  the Phone app's CallSynergizer talks to, registered with LSRegister
  when the plugin loads, so it is on the bus before the Phone app
  subscribes at boot. It tells audiod about the call with
  CallStatusUpdate, so the call devices the engine uses are routed.
- libteams.c: register the service at load and when an account logs
  in; on teams_close, end the account's call and unbind it from the
  service before its connections are cancelled.
- teams_trouter.c: register the personal calling endpoint
  (SkypeSpacesWeb, TFL context, registrationId = epid, at
  teams.microsoft.com), route /callAgent/ and bare-surl frames to the call
  handler, renew registrations every 5 minutes instead of once a day
  (call routing went stale long before 24 h), and log registrar
  responses.
- Makefile: with TEAMS_WEBOS_CALL=1, build teams_calling.c and
  teams_call_luna.c into libteams-personal.so, with -DTEAMS_WEBOS_CALL,
  -DTEAMS_MEDIA_BIN from TEAMS_MEDIA_BIN and luna-service2. Only that
  plugin gets calling, so only one registers com.palm.teams.call.

Without TEAMS_WEBOS_CALL the trouter still prints the "Incoming call"
message as upstream does, and teams_call_log() compiles to nothing.
Before this, a build with the upstream Makefile left
teams_calling_handle_trouter and teams_call_log undefined in the plugin,
so libpurple could not load it.

Signed-off-by: Herman van Hazendonk <github.com@herrie.org>
Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [webOS specific]
